This commit's coinbase.rs hunk (+97/-3) is a standalone fix, unrelated to the
v7.1.88 release it landed inside of — it was swept in by a concurrent commit
in this shared tree, not authored as part of the release.

fix(sigil-node): pool-share coinbase credits now honor shield-registration

split_coinbase_mutations — the path essentially every real block win goes
through once external miners are active — credited every recipient with a
plain transparent SetBalance, with no check for shield-registration at all.
The shield-aware ShieldedCoinbase logic added 2026-08-23 (654c0d7) only lived
in the legacy single-producer build_block_body_for, which is reached only on
the increasingly-rare no-solve fallback — so registering a wallet for
shielded rewards had no effect on a real miner's actual winnings. (654c0d7's
own message flagged this: "Registration also needs a SigilTx variant + API
route before a real miner can use it; that is the next step, not this one.")

Reuses the existing coinbase_commitment_wire domain (height as the
separator) rather than inventing a new one: split_coinbase_mutations runs
at most once per height and every recipient in one call is a distinct
wallet, so no new collision surface is introduced. Falls back to the exact
prior transparent credit when unregistered or the amount exceeds the
shielded circuit's representable range — no existing miner's payout changes.

Verified: two new tests (registered miner mints a shielded note with correct
native/shielded conservation; unregistered miner byte-identical to prior
behavior) plus all 10 other coinbase-module tests green, including the
multi-node determinism/conservation gates. One pre-existing failure in the
same file (send_applies_in_block_and_is_deterministic) confirmed via stash
A/B to be unrelated and pre-existing. Not deployed to the live producer.

